WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
A car cruises along a flat
road at a steady speed.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.830
A driving force pushes it forwards.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.650
Friction and air resistance
push backwards, just as hard.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.670
The forces are balanced.

5
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.790
So shouldn't the car
slow down and stop?

6
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.770
Or is something else going on?

7
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.130
In this mission, you'll find
out what a force really is,

8
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.490
and why every force needs two objects.

9
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.650
You'll sort contact
and non-contact forces.

10
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.310
You'll stretch springs, and
see how they measure force.

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.550
Then you'll find out
what balanced forces do.

12
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.470
Your mission: explain why a car
with balanced forces doesn't

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.460
stop.
